WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:04.350
The plateau photograph shows cliffs, ledges and softer slopes.

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:07.550
These are modern expressions of differing rock resistance.

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:11.210
The gray slope and tan cliffs help locate units, but exact

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:14.890
depositional settings require the supplied column, textures and fossils.

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:18.750
The investigation has four numbered units, with unit four oldest at

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:20.750
the bottom and unit one youngest at the top.

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:26.410
Unit four includes rounded pebbles, coarse sand, wood, plant-bearing mudstone and

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:30.690
dinosaur tracks. Together they support a river system and floodplain.

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:33.350
This is not the dune sandstone at the base of a

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:37.610
different Connect sequence. Always identify which source column is being interpreted

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:39.270
before transferring an answer.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:43.990
Unit three has yellow-tan quartz sandstone with marine shell fragments.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:48.190
Its basal conglomerate cuts an erosion surface and locally includes wood

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:50.890
and leaves, supporting beach and river influence.

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:55.410
Overlying unit two is organic-rich gray shale with marine fossils and

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:59.510
local limestone. This change from land through shoreline toward marine mud

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:00.770
supports a transgression.

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:05.530
Upper unit one starts with shell-bearing tan sandstone and passes into

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:08.950
sandstone, mudstone, plants, mudcracks and coal.

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:12.750
Shoreline or delta deposition gave way to coastal land and wetlands.

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:15.990
That upward change above marine shale supports regression.

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:19.990
The upper package is sandstone and mudstone with coal, not a

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:21.190
reef limestone cap.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:27.450
From oldest to youngest, the sequence records river and floodplain, shoreline

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:31.090
sand, marine mud, then shoreline and coastal land.

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:34.550
The whole record is a transgression followed by a regression.

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:38.190
The lower yellow-tan sandstone is compared with the Dakota in the

00:01:38.190 --> 00:01:42.630
Denver example. Give observations for each interpretation rather than treating a

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:44.710
matching name as independent proof.
